description:
Programme duration: from 3 to 6 months, starting in 2027.

Who qualifies: Penultimate or final year students completing a Bachelor's, Master's, PhD.

Qube Research &amp; Technologies (QRT) is a global quantitative and systematic investment manager, operating in all liquid asset classes across the world. We are a technology and data driven group implementing a scientific approach to investing. Combining data, research, technology, and trading expertise has shaped our collaborative mindset which enables us to solve the most complex challenges. QRT’s culture of innovation continuously drives our ambition to deliver high quality returns for our investors.

&nbsp;

Over the years, QRT has invested in a global research and execution platform which has been deployed to cover all geographies and asset classes. This platform covers a broad spectrum from high to low frequency trading systems. We thrive at the intersection of cutting-edge technology, smart automation, and scalable processes, enabling us to move fast, think big, and deliver at scale.

We are committed to identifying and developing exceptional talent, and are inviting a new cohort of outstanding individuals to join us in the year ahead. Our internship offers a stimulating, intellectually rigorous, and high-performance environment, where collaboration is key to success. You will work alongside and be mentored by industry-leading professionals, gaining invaluable experience and positioning yourself for the opportunity to secure a full-time graduate role upon successful completion of the program.

&nbsp;

Data Engineer

Manage extensive datasets across QRT’s research and trading platforms. Design and implement data stores and APIs, monitor the health and performance of data processes, and deliver production-ready datasets. Provide direct support to Researchers and Traders to ensure they can fully leverage the capabilities of our data platform. &nbsp;

Your present skillset   &nbsp;

• Strong core computer science foundations, including algorithms, data structures, parallel programming, and object-oriented programming (OOP).&nbsp;

• Genuine interest in software engineering, infrastructure, or data engineering within a low-latency environment, working in Python.

• Interest to build expertise in high-performance, real-time trading systems&nbsp;

• Excellent communication and analytical skills - you will interact directly with Traders and Researchers &nbsp;

• Drive for rapid autonomy and the ability to work in a fast-paced, high-performance setting.&nbsp;

• Rigorous and structured approach to problem-solving.&nbsp;

Preferred qualifications (a plus): &nbsp;

• Knowledge of databases such as SQL or NoSQL. &nbsp;

• Experience in front-end development.

• Interest in financial markets and/or algorithmic trading.&nbsp;

Interview Process:

• Application - Submit your application online. We review applications on a rolling basis, so we recommend applying early to maximize your chances.

• Technical Assessment - Selected candidates will be invited to complete a coding challenge designed to evaluate core technical and problem-solving skills. &nbsp;

• Interviews - Shortlisted applicants will proceed to interviews conducted either on-site or via Microsoft Teams. These will assess both your technical expertise and your alignment with our culture and values.

QRT is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome diversity as essential to our success. QRT empowers employees to work openly and respectfully to achieve collective success. In addition to professional achievement, we are offering initiatives and programs to enable employees achieve a healthy work-life balance &nbsp;

About Grupo QuintoAndar

We are Grupo QuintoAndar, the largest real estate ecosystem in Latin America. Guided by a shared purpose of helping people love where they live, we have a diversified portfolio of brands and solutions across different countries in Latin America, covering all phases of the housing journey. We also have a Technology Hub in Portugal. We develop technology and innovation to transform and enhance the overall living experience.

With the support of a world-class team of investors and advisors, including Kaszek, Qualcomm, General Atlantic, and SoftBank, Grupo QuintoAndar is currently valued at over USD 5.1 billion and continues to grow year over year.

Here, you will work with top professionals in the market, in an environment that breathes innovation, collaboration, and high performance. To learn more about our story, visit: https://grupoquintoandar.com/pt/ .

&nbsp;

Why is this position affirmatively focused on people with disabilities?

Grupo QuintoAndar is committed to promoting Social Inclusion, and one of our key pillars is representation within our teams. By creating more opportunities and taking intentional action, we can advance the development and strengthening of social inclusion in our workplace.
It is essential to note that our hiring process for this position remains unchanged in terms of stages and evaluation methods. We understand that recruitment is a gateway to diversity, and we are always attentive to what makes us plural.

&nbsp;

Location &amp; Hybrid Work Model for hybrid positions

Our team follows a “hybrid” model, requiring in-person attendance at our office located in São Paulo.

&nbsp;

Hiring Process Stages

The stages of our hiring processes aim to assess your experiences and allow you to meet our teams and explore career opportunities. They are structured as follows:

• Submitting your application;

• Validation of a disability medical report;

• People Interview;

• Hiring Manager Interview;

• Case;

• Stakeholder Interview;

• Offer!

About the Team

QuintoAndar is seeking a hands-on, highly organized, and detail-oriented Fintech Regulatory Specialist to join our Legal &amp; Regulatory team. As we verticalize our financial stack and secure our institutional autonomy, this role will serve as the strategic technical architect and expert for our regulatory compliance infrastructure. Working with technical full autonomy, you will design scalable compliance systems, serve as an internal advisor across the Legal Org and senior leadership, and leverage modern AI and automation tools to drive high-speed regulatory execution.&nbsp;

Key Responsibilities

• Regulatory Project Management: Design, implement, and maintain robust, audit-proof compliance frameworks across Central Bank (BCB) licensing pipelines (SCFI and Consórcio). Build scalable processes that enable peer execution while mentoring less experienced lawyers on the team.&nbsp;

• Reporting &amp; Data Infrastructure: Reporting Strategy &amp; Automation: Architect, automate, and oversee data infrastructure for mandatory BCB reporting (STA, Unicad, Sisorf, Document 2080), ensuring long-term systemic reliability and data integrity while overseeing operational execution.&nbsp;

• Cross-Functional Alignment: Functional Alignment: Serve as the primary regulatory advisor for Product, Tech, Finance (COSIF), and Compliance. Evaluate complex, multi-variable legal scenarios to create scalable regulatory strategies that unlock business opportunities while mitigating institutional risk.&nbsp;

• Routine Inquiries &amp; Research: Leverage AI and modern tech tools to deliver rapid, high-impact synthesis on evolving BCB frameworks (e.g., CP 108/BaaS). Act as QuintoAndar's primary representative in key industry forums, contributing directly to public consultations and market policy discussions.&nbsp;

Qualifications &amp; Requirements

• Education: Law degree with 8+ years with post-graduation experience and active OAB registration. A Postgrad

&nbsp;

ABOUT US

Capco is a global technology and management consultancy specializing in driving digital transformation in the financial services and insurance industries. Capco is committed to providing clients with practical solutions. We offer a globally integrated service with offices in leading financial centers across the globe. We have the people, the vision, and the passion.

We are growing through a significant growth journey, now is a very good time to join us as we expand geographically, increase headcount and disrupt the consulting market across APAC with entrepreneurial and agile thinking.

We are:

• Experts in banking and payments, capital markets and wealth and asset management

• Deep knowledge in financial services offering, including e.g. Finance, Risk and Compliance, Financial Crime, Core Banking etc.

• Committed to growing our business and hiring the best talent to help us get there

• Focus on maintaining our nimble, agile and entrepreneurial culture

&nbsp;

ROLE RESPONSIBILITIES

We are currently seeking multiple consultants and senior consultants to support and drive the growth of our Data practice, particularly in our Data governance and data management stream. This is an exciting opportunity to be a leader, in a growing team of data practitioners, where you will be initiating and implementing cutting-edge data &amp; analytics programmes for top-tier Financial Services clients.

This project is with a leading bank as a Business Analyst / Project Manager for Data governance and management project&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

KEY RESPONSIBILITIES&nbsp;

• Implement and maintain data governance frameworks, policies, standards, and best practices across the organization.

• Assisting to drive data quality initiatives, including defining controls, monitoring KPIs, and coordinating issue remediation.

• Support data ownership, stewardship, metadata management, and data lineage processes.

• Partner with business, technology, risk, and compliance stakeholders to ensure effective governance and regulatory compliance.

• Facilitate governance forums, stakeholder engagement, and training to promote data governance adoption.

• Support audit, regulatory, and enterprise data transformation initiatives through strong data management practices.

SKILLS &amp; EXPERTISE

• 3+ years of experience in Data Governance, Data Management , or data quality within financial services&nbsp;

• Good understanding of data governance, data quality, metadata management, and data lineage concepts.

• Experience on supporting and defining data strategies, target-state operating models , data capabilities, and implementation roadmaps to support business transformation and data-driven decision-making.

• Familiarity with data enablement process and delivered different strategies for refinement and improvement&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Excellent stakeholder management, communication, problem-solving, and analytical skills.

• Experience within Banking, Financial Services, Consulting, or other highly regulated environments is preferred

• SQL and relevant data governance certifications are advantageous.

ELIGIBILITY TO WORK IN SG

Applicants must have unrestricted working rights in Singapore. Only Singapore Citizens and Singapore Permanent Residents (PRs) will be considered. Employment Pass sponsorship is not available for this role.

&nbsp;

WHY CAPCO?  &nbsp;

We are expanding our business rapidly across Singapore and Asia. You will work on engaging projects with some of the largest banking and insurance clients in the world, projects that will deliver significant transformation and change.

